## Why This Is Asked
This tests automation, Vault + SPIFFE integration, and zero-downtime trust reconfiguration across DCs.

## Key Concepts
- Vault CA bundles and SPIFFE trust anchors
- SPIFFE SVID rotation and edge-proxy hot-reload
- Idempotence, rollback, and verification across DCs

## Code Example
```javascript
// bootstrap trust distribution (pseudocode)
async function bootstrapCrossDC(dc) {
  await fetchTrustAnchors(dc);
  await rotateSVIDs(dc);
  await hotReloadProxies(dc);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test drift between trust material and service SVIDs?
- How do you handle partial failures during bootstrap (e.g., one DC unreachable)?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to add a real, cross-DC capability using Docker Configs, a TLS edge (Traefik), and a simple stateful component (Redis). It also touches observability (metrics) and inter-DC consistency via pub/sub.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant rate limiting with Redis counters
- Docker Configs for per-tenant quotas
- Cross-DC synchronization via Redis Pub/Sub
- TLS termination with Traefik edge proxy
- Metrics exposure for Prometheus

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-rate-limit middleware sketch
const quota = getQuotaFromConfig(req.headers['X-Tenant']);
const key = `rl:${tenant}:${windowStart}`;
let count = redis.incr(key);
if (count === 1) redis.expire(key, windowSeconds);
if (count > quota) {
  res.status(429).set('Retry-After', String(windowSeconds)).send('Too Many Requests');
} else {
  next();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test burst traffic and quota drift across DCs?
- What strategies ensure accurate time windows across replicas?
- How would you monitor per-tenant usage and alert on anomalies?
